{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/648206-how-does-mnesis-work-for-mokole","id":648206,"title":"How does Mnesis work for Mokole?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-01T11:45:29-07:00","id":648206,"title":"How does Mnesis work for Mokole?","content":"I have a story telling question on how Mnesis works. It\u2019s a big part of the Mokole, but there doesn\u2019t seem to be much that explains what goes on when they use it. I\u2019ve heard references to \u201cMnesis Quests\u201d but I\u2019m struggling to get the right feel for it. Does the Mokole actually have control during the memory? Can they fight, and do things while in their trance? Is it almost like navigating the Umbra and dealing with spirits? Or is it really just a memory, and the Mokole describes what they want to do, make their Mnesis roll, and then I just describe to them what the memory is?<br /> <br /> In my mind, I was imagining it almost like a dreamstate where the Mokole would have some control over what\u2019s going on and must actually find what they\u2019re looking for in the memory, but I have no idea if that\u2019s an accurate representation of what it is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T11:52:00-07:00","id":648226,"title":"","content":"Those are all excellent ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T17:35:23-07:00","id":648477,"title":"","content":"I always considered Mnemsis to be a pretty active thing- where the Mokole tangibly relives the old memories. When the Mnemetics were described in the 20th BotW, they became addicted to altering their own memories, changing what was 'true' to their liking. Instead of reliving what happened accurately in order to learn or celebrate or mourn, the Mnetics get off on playing god (their corrupt memory quests resembling Neo running amok in the Matrix) as they remake and alter the events of the past to suit their liking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T01:36:02-07:00","id":656219,"title":"","content":"Mnesis is a narrative tool above anyting. The point of Mnesis is to add a touch of mystery and discovery to the chronicle. It's not something that can be ever really controlled by a single character but is a product of the character cooperating with the ST. A number of my players really love Mokole to bits, but not everyone really enjoys mucking about with Mnesis.<br /> <br /> Considering that Mnesis are a pool of joint memories and experiences of things all the past Mokole have experienced you have quite a bit of options there:<br /> <br /> - the character is likely to use it to get information and skills through a game<br /> - it can be used as a way to commune with old Mokole who can serve as mentors, guides or allies<br /> - it can be used as a way to quest into the hallways of memory where you might end up fighting or outwitting the guardians of memories or dredging long lost secrets. This works especially well when you combine it with a quest to actually explore the places and items related to the memory, which sparks further ideas and recognition. I've even used it as a way to raise Mnesis, and as a way to showcase locations and characters the players are encountering in a different light<br /> - the quest can also take the form of communion between multiple Mokole to explore a topic from different sides, allowing you to create a lovely little Rashamoniad<br /> - my favourite interpretation of the quest comes from a joint mnesis quest with the whole cast, even if they are not Mokole - you have each and every one of the PC's transported back in time as different yet familiar characters and exploring the context of the current storyline and what led to it<br /> <br /> It's an amazing tool, really. It's down to you (And the willingness of your Mokole players) how much you will end up using it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T03:32:19-07:00","id":656309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/648206-how-does-mnesis-work-for-mokole?p=648477#post648477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always considered Mnemsis to be a pretty active thing- where the Mokole tangibly relives the old memories. When the Mnemetics were described in the 20th BotW, they became addicted to altering their own memories, changing what was 'true' to their liking. Instead of reliving what happened accurately in order to learn or celebrate or mourn, the Mnetics get off on playing god (their corrupt memory quests resembling Neo running amok in the Matrix) as they remake and alter the events of the past to suit their liking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you like the Mnetics <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm of the opinion you could run whole sessions (or even whole campaigns) within the Mnesis, much as described above - living within the fluidity of memory, Matrix-style. Fighting Mnetics who want to corrupt the living memory. Restoring the balance and bringing the Mnesis back to what other Mokole agree was the true history. Does this healing change what was previously remembered?<br /> <br /> Hmm, I've just sensed a Shattered Dreams Kickstarter stretch goal somewhere in all this...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T13:19:01-07:00","id":659774,"title":"","content":"Thank you everyone for the replies! This has been very helpful. Now hopefully when I do this game I'll be able to do the Mnesis justice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T06:09:41-07:00","id":1559716,"title":"","content":"I love the alternate idea put forth in <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, wherein the Mnesis that the Mokol\u00e9 possess isn't some sacred duty that is vital to Gaia, but rather a punishment from Gaia for what their Wonder Workers did to destroy the original Mnesis, from the corpse of which the Weaver wove the Gauntlet. Of course, going by that one, the Mokol\u00e9 are absolute shits, and while the Garou didn't know a thing about the failure of the proto-Mokol\u00e9, they inevitably (and accidentally) acted as Gaia's ultimate justice by giving them their overdue executions. I think it's great that the Mnesis is a punishment, designed to remind them of their utter failure, and it makes Me wonder if their purpose under Gaia, beyond simply existing in eternal punishment, is to guide the other Changing Breeds to not share in the hubris of the proto-Mokol\u00e9.<br /> <br /> I'd love to play the Mnesis 5 Mokol\u00e9 that managed to find the memories of how they received the Mnesis in the first place, and who realises that the entire Changing Breed are Gaia's greatest disappointment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T17:33:26-07:00","id":1559740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Vil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/648206-how-does-mnesis-work-for-mokole?p=1559716#post1559716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the alternate idea put forth in <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, wherein the Mnesis that the Mokol\u00e9 possess isn't some sacred duty that is vital to Gaia, but rather a punishment from Gaia for what their Wonder Workers did to destroy the original Mnesis, from the corpse of which the Weaver wove the Gauntlet. Of course, going by that one, the Mokol\u00e9 are absolute shits, and while the Garou didn't know a thing about the failure of the proto-Mokol\u00e9, they inevitably (and accidentally) acted as Gaia's ultimate justice by giving them their overdue executions. I think it's great that the Mnesis is a punishment, designed to remind them of their utter failure, and it makes Me wonder if their purpose under Gaia, beyond simply existing in eternal punishment, is to guide the other Changing Breeds to not share in the hubris of the proto-Mokol\u00e9.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great idea! Let's take it to its logical conclusion! So you know, you're charged in culpability for something unspeakable that an <i>Australopithecus</i> did before living memory. Sentence rendered is to be slid down a pike, to be carried out immediately after finding the party guilty (the verdict is pre-determined).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd love to play the Mnesis 5 Mokol\u00e9 that managed to find the memories of how they received the Mnesis in the first place, and who realises that the entire Changing Breed are Gaia's greatest disappointment. </div> </div> </div>You wouldn't need more than four dots. That gets you to The Asteroid and just a bit before. Also, I'm pretty sure they would all mostly know it already. That's the whole thing about being the Memory; it's their job to recall it so that future generations don't do it again. The only reason it's not mentioned in Mokole is because that book pre-dates the concept of &quot;But what if the Mokole had a terrible failure in their past?&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, this just gives the Mokole more heat and proves that they should be the protagonists of the setting. Get ready for Weresaurian: The Eternity!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}